      "id": 65919,
      "name": "arenson9",
      "username": "arenson9",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-06-15T16:54:43.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"lynkfox\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lynkfox/48/1997_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> lynkfox:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p><em>EDIT</em>&nbsp;waityou wanted the smaller cards&nbsp;no, i do not believe the promo villians even /have/ a smaller card.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Baron Blade and Cosmic Omnitron made up four of the six promo cards (with Beard Ra and Redeemer Fanatic) that were first made available during the EE/IR Kickstarter and were later made available at cons via Sentinels Points. They may have also been made available during the ST Kickstarter, though I don't recall for sure. I <em>think</em> they are no longer available from &gt;G.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Don't know if anyone has uploaded front/back pictures of them for printing – it's not something I've paid much attention to.</p>",
      "post_number": 6,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:43:28.756Z",
